{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# KubeRay Cluster Test - OpenShift AI Compatible\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook tests Ray cluster creation using **KubeRay** with OpenShift AI / ODH compatible configuration.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Workflow:**\n",
    "1. Create RayCluster resource\n",
    "2. Wait for cluster ready\n",
    "3. Get dashboard URL\n",
    "4. **Press Enter** to delete\n",
    "\n",
    "**Prerequisites:**\n",
    "- KubeRay operator installed\n",
    "- Access to your namespace (update `YOUR_NAMESPACE` below)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Note:** This configuration matches the OpenShift AI / CodeFlare style with proper images and certificate handling."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Configuration\n",
    "\n",
    "**Update these values for your environment:**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================================\n",
    "# CONFIGURATION - UPDATE THESE VALUES\n",
    "# ============================================================================\n",
    "\n",
    "NAMESPACE = \"user-mhepburn\"  # Change to your namespace\n",
    "CLUSTER_NAME = \"test-ray-cluster\"\n",
    "NUM_WORKERS = 2\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set to True if you have GPU nodes with tolerations/selectors\n",
    "USE_GPU = False  # Set to True for GPU workers\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"✓ Configuration:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Namespace: {NAMESPACE}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Cluster: {CLUSTER_NAME}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Workers: {NUM_WORKERS}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  GPU: {USE_GPU}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1: Define the RayCluster Configuration\n",
    "\n",
    "This configuration matches OpenShift AI / CodeFlare patterns:\n",
    "- Uses CodeFlare Ray image: `quay.io/project-codeflare/ray:latest-py39-cu118`\n",
    "- Ray version: `2.54.1`\n",
    "- Includes ODH trusted CA certificate mounts\n",
    "- Disables Ray usage stats\n",
    "- Includes proper lifecycle hooks"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import subprocess\n",
    "import time\n",
    "import yaml\n",
    "\n",
    "# Helper volumes for ODH trusted CA (optional but recommended)\n",
    "odh_volumes = [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        \"name\": \"odh-trusted-ca-cert\",\n",
    "        \"configMap\": {\n",
    "            \"name\": \"odh-trusted-ca-bundle\",\n",
    "            \"items\": [{\"key\": \"ca-bundle.crt\", \"path\": \"odh-trusted-ca-bundle.crt\"}],\n",
    "            \"optional\": True\n",
    "        }\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        \"name\": \"odh-ca-cert\",\n",
    "        \"configMap\": {\n",
    "            \"name\": \"odh-trusted-ca-bundle\",\n",
    "            \"items\": [{\"key\": \"odh-ca-bundle.crt\", \"path\": \"odh-ca-bundle.crt\"}],\n",
    "            \"optional\": True\n",
    "        }\n",
    "    }\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Helper volume mounts for ODH trusted CA\n",
    "odh_volume_mounts = [\n",
    "    {\"mountPath\": \"/etc/pki/tls/certs/odh-trusted-ca-bundle.crt\",\n",
    "     \"name\": \"odh-trusted-ca-cert\", \"subPath\": \"odh-trusted-ca-bundle.crt\"},\n",
    "    {\"mountPath\": \"/etc/ssl/certs/odh-trusted-ca-bundle.crt\",\n",
    "     \"name\": \"odh-trusted-ca-cert\", \"subPath\": \"odh-trusted-ca-bundle.crt\"},\n",
    "    {\"mountPath\": \"/etc/pki/tls/certs/odh-ca-bundle.crt\",\n",
    "     \"name\": \"odh-ca-cert\", \"subPath\": \"odh-ca-bundle.crt\"},\n",
    "    {\"mountPath\": \"/etc/ssl/certs/odh-ca-bundle.crt\",\n",
    "     \"name\": \"odh-ca-cert\", \"subPath\": \"odh-ca-bundle.crt\"},\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Define the RayCluster configuration (OpenShift AI / CodeFlare style)\n",
    "cluster_config = {\n",
    "    \"apiVersion\": \"ray.io/v1\",\n",
    "    \"kind\": \"RayCluster\",\n",
    "    \"metadata\": {\n",
    "        \"name\": CLUSTER_NAME,\n",
    "        \"namespace\": NAMESPACE,\n",
    "        \"annotations\": {\n",
    "            \"odh.ray.io/secure-trusted-network\": \"true\"\n",
    "        }\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"spec\": {\n",
    "        \"rayVersion\": \"2.54.1\",\n",
    "        \"enableInTreeAutoscaling\": False,\n",
    "        \"headGroupSpec\": {\n",
    "            \"serviceType\": \"ClusterIP\",\n",
    "            \"enableIngress\": False,\n",
    "            \"rayStartParams\": {\n",
    "                \"dashboard-host\": \"0.0.0.0\",\n",
    "                \"block\": \"true\",\n",
    "                \"num-gpus\": \"0\"\n",
    "            },\n",
    "            \"template\": {\n",
    "                \"spec\": {\n",
    "                    \"containers\": [{\n",
    "                        \"name\": \"ray-head\",\n",
    "                        \"image\": \"quay.io/project-codeflare/ray:latest-py39-cu118\",\n",
    "                        \"imagePullPolicy\": \"Always\",\n",
    "                        \"env\": [\n",
    "                            {\"name\": \"RAY_USAGE_STATS_ENABLED\", \"value\": \"0\"}\n",
    "                        ],\n",
    "                        \"ports\": [\n",
    "                            {\"containerPort\": 6379, \"name\": \"gcs\", \"protocol\": \"TCP\"},\n",
    "                            {\"containerPort\": 8265, \"name\": \"dashboard\", \"protocol\": \"TCP\"},\n",
    "                            {\"containerPort\": 10001, \"name\": \"client\", \"protocol\": \"TCP\"}\n",
    "                        ],\n",
    "                        \"resources\": {\n",
    "                            \"limits\": {\"cpu\": \"2\", \"memory\": \"8G\"},\n",
    "                            \"requests\": {\"cpu\": \"1\", \"memory\": \"5G\"}\n",
    "                        },\n",
    "                        \"lifecycle\": {\n",
    "                            \"preStop\": {\n",
    "                                \"exec\": {\"command\": [\"/bin/sh\", \"-c\", \"ray stop\"]}\n",
    "                            }\n",
    "                        },\n",
    "                        \"volumeMounts\": odh_volume_mounts\n",
    "                    }],\n",
    "                    \"volumes\": odh_volumes\n",
    "                }\n",
    "            }\n",
    "        },\n",
    "        \"workerGroupSpecs\": [{\n",
    "            \"replicas\": NUM_WORKERS,\n",
    "            \"minReplicas\": NUM_WORKERS,\n",
    "            \"maxReplicas\": NUM_WORKERS,\n",
    "            \"groupName\": \"worker-group\",\n",
    "            \"rayStartParams\": {\n",
    "                \"block\": \"true\",\n",
    "                \"num-gpus\": \"1\" if USE_GPU else \"0\"\n",
    "            },\n",
    "            \"template\": {\n",
    "                \"spec\": {\n",
    "                    \"containers\": [{\n",
    "                        \"name\": \"ray-worker\",\n",
    "                        \"image\": \"quay.io/project-codeflare/ray:latest-py39-cu118\",\n",
    "                        \"imagePullPolicy\": \"Always\",\n",
    "                        \"env\": [\n",
    "                            {\"name\": \"RAY_USAGE_STATS_ENABLED\", \"value\": \"0\"}\n",
    "                        ],\n",
    "                        \"resources\": {\n",
    "                            \"limits\": {\n",
    "                                \"cpu\": \"2\" if USE_GPU else \"1\",\n",
    "                                \"memory\": \"8G\" if USE_GPU else \"6G\",\n",
    "                                **({\"nvidia.com/gpu\": \"1\"} if USE_GPU else {})\n",
    "                            },\n",
    "                            \"requests\": {\n",
    "                                \"cpu\": \"1\",\n",
    "                                \"memory\": \"4G\" if USE_GPU else \"3G\",\n",
    "                                **({\"nvidia.com/gpu\": \"1\"} if USE_GPU else {})\n",
    "                            }\n",
    "                        },\n",
    "                        \"lifecycle\": {\n",
    "                            \"preStop\": {\n",
    "                                \"exec\": {\"command\": [\"/bin/sh\", \"-c\", \"ray stop\"]}\n",
    "                            }\n",
    "                        },\n",
    "                        \"volumeMounts\": odh_volume_mounts\n",
    "                    }],\n",
    "                    \"volumes\": odh_volumes\n",
    "                }\n",
    "            }\n",
    "        }]\n",
    "    }\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Write to temp file\n",
    "cluster_yaml_path = \"/tmp/test-ray-cluster.yaml\"\n",
    "with open(cluster_yaml_path, 'w') as f:
    "    yaml.dump(cluster_config, f)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n✓ RayCluster configuration prepared\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Name: {CLUSTER_NAME}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Namespace: {NAMESPACE}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Workers: {NUM_WORKERS}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Image: quay.io/project-codeflare/ray:latest-py39-cu118\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Ray Version: 2.54.1\")\n",
    "print(f\"  GPU: {USE_GPU}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nConfiguration written to: {cluster_yaml_path}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2: Create the RayCluster"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def run_kubectl(args, check=True):
    "    \"\"\"Helper to run kubectl commands\"\"\"\n",
    "    result = subprocess.run(\n",
    "        [\"kubectl\"] + args,\n",
    "        capture_output=True,\n",
    "        text=True\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    if check and result.returncode != 0:\n",
    "        raise Exception(f\"kubectl failed: {result.stderr}\")\n",
    "    return result\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Creating RayCluster...\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "result = run_kubectl([\"apply\", \"-f\", cluster_yaml_path])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✓ RayCluster created successfully!\")\n",
    "print(result.stdout)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3: Wait for Cluster to be Ready\n",
    "\n",
    "This will wait for all pods to be Running."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def wait_for_cluster_ready(timeout=600):
    "    \"\"\"Wait for Ray cluster pods to be ready\"\"\"\n",
    "    print(\"Waiting for Ray cluster to be ready...\")\n",
    "    print(\"This may take 2-5 minutes for:\")\n",
    "    print(\"  - Image pulls (CodeFlare Ray image)\")\n",
    "    print(\"  - Pod scheduling\")\n",
    "    print(\"  - Container initialization\\n\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    start_time = time.time()\n",
    "    expected_pods = 1 + NUM_WORKERS  # head + workers\n",
    "    \n",
    "    while time.time() - start_time < timeout:\n",
    "        elapsed = int(time.time() - start_time)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Get pod status\n",
    "        result = run_kubectl([\n",
    "            \"get\", \"pods\",\n",
    "            \"-n\", NAMESPACE,\n",
    "            \"-l\", f\"ray.io/cluster={CLUSTER_NAME}\",\n",
    "            \"--no-headers\"\n",
    "        ], check=False)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        if result.returncode == 0:\n",
    "            lines = result.stdout.strip().split('\\n')\n",
    "            if lines and lines[0]:  # Has pods\n",
    "                total = len(lines)\n",
    "                running = sum(1 for line in lines if 'Running' in line and '1/1' in line)\n",
    "                \n",
    "                print(f\"\\r[{elapsed:3d}s] Pods ready: {running}/{expected_pods}\", end=\"\", flush=True)\n",
    "                \n",
    "                if running >= expected_pods:\n",
    "                    print(f\"\\n\\n✓ Ray cluster is ready! (took {elapsed}s)\")\n",
    "                    return True\n",
    "        \n",
    "        time.sleep(5)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(f\"\\n\\n⚠ Timeout after {timeout}s\")\n",
    "    return False\n",
    "\n",
    "ready = wait_for_cluster_ready()\n",
    "\n",
    "if not ready:\n",
    "    print(\"\\nCluster may still be starting. Check status manually:\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  kubectl get pods -n {NAMESPACE} -l ray.io/cluster={CLUSTER_NAME}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 4: Get Cluster Details and Dashboard URL"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def get_cluster_details():
    "    \"\"\"Get RayCluster status and connection info\"\"\"\n",
    "    print(\"=\" * 80)\n",
    "    print(\"RAY CLUSTER DETAILS\")\n",
    "    print(\"=\" * 80)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # RayCluster resource\n",
    "    print(\"\\n📋 RayCluster Resource:\\n\")\n",
    "    result = run_kubectl([\"get\", \"raycluster\", CLUSTER_NAME, \"-n\", NAMESPACE])\n",
    "    print(result.stdout)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Pods\n",
    "    print(\"\\n🚀 Pods:\\n\")\n",
    "    result = run_kubectl([\n",
    "        \"get\", \"pods\",\n",
    "        \"-n\", NAMESPACE,\n",
    "        \"-l\", f\"ray.io/cluster={CLUSTER_NAME}\"\n",
    "    ])\n",
    "    print(result.stdout)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Services\n",
    "    print(\"\\n🌐 Services:\\n\")\n",
    "    result = run_kubectl([\n",
    "        \"get\", \"svc\",\n",
    "        \"-n\", NAMESPACE,\n",
    "        \"-l\", f\"ray.io/cluster={CLUSTER_NAME}\"\n",
    "    ])\n",
    "    print(result.stdout)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(\"=\" * 80)\n",
    "\n",
    "get_cluster_details()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 5: Get Dashboard URL"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def get_dashboard_url():
    "    \"\"\"Get Ray dashboard URL\"\"\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Get head service\n",
    "    result = run_kubectl([\n",
    "        \"get\", \"svc\",\n",
    "        \"-n\", NAMESPACE,\n",
    "        \"-l\", f\"ray.io/cluster={CLUSTER_NAME},ray.io/node-type=head\",\n",
    "        \"-o\", \"jsonpath={.items[0].metadata.name}\"\n",
    "    ])\n",
    "    \n",
    "    service_name = result.stdout.strip()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    if not service_name:\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Connection URIs\n",
    "    cluster_uri = f\"ray://{service_name}.{NAMESPACE}.svc.cluster.local:10001\"\n",
    "    dashboard_internal = f\"http://{service_name}.{NAMESPACE}.svc.cluster.local:8265\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"service_name\": service_name,\n",
    "        \"cluster_uri\": cluster_uri,\n",
    "        \"dashboard_internal\": dashboard_internal,\n",
    "        \"dashboard_port\": 8265\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "urls = get_dashboard_url()\n",
    "\n",
    "if urls:\n",
    "    print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 80)\n",
    "    print(\"CONNECTION INFORMATION\")\n",
    "    print(\"=\" * 80)\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n📊 Ray Cluster URI (for ray.init):\")\n",
    "    print(f\"   {urls['cluster_uri']}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n📈 Ray Dashboard:\")\n",
    "    print(f\"   Internal: {urls['dashboard_internal']}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n💡 To access dashboard from your laptop:\")\n",
    "    print(f\"   kubectl port-forward svc/{urls['service_name']} {urls['dashboard_port']}:8265 -n {NAMESPACE}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"   Then open: http://localhost:{urls['dashboard_port']}\")\n",
    "    print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 80)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"⚠ Could not find head service\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 6: Pause - Press Enter to Delete\n",
    "\n",
    "**The cluster is running!**\n",
    "\n",
    "You can:\n",
    "- Port-forward the dashboard and verify it works\n",
    "- Check pod details\n",
    "- Test ray.init() connection (if Ray is installed)\n",
    "\n",
    "Press Enter when ready to clean up."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"\\n\" + \"⚠\" * 40)\n",
    "print(\"\\n🛑 Ray cluster is RUNNING\")\n",
    "print(\"\\nCluster Info:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Name: {CLUSTER_NAME}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Namespace: {NAMESPACE}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Workers: {NUM_WORKERS}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  GPU: {USE_GPU}\")\n",
    "if urls:\n",
    "    print(f\"  Service: {urls['service_name']}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Dashboard port-forward: {urls['dashboard_port']}\")\n",
    "print(\"\\nTake your time to verify everything works.\")\n",
    "print(\"\\nWhen ready to clean up, press ENTER...\")\n",
    "print(\"\\n\" + \"⚠\" * 40 + \"\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "input(\"Press ENTER to delete the cluster >>> \")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n✓ Proceeding with cleanup...\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 7: Delete the RayCluster"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Deleting RayCluster...\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "result = run_kubectl([\"delete\", \"-f\", cluster_yaml_path])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✓ RayCluster deleted!\")\n",
    "print(result.stdout)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 8: Verify Cleanup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def verify_cleanup(timeout=120):
    "    \"\"\"Verify all resources are cleaned up\"\"\"\n",
    "    print(\"Waiting for cleanup to complete...\\n\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    start_time = time.time()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    while time.time() - start_time < timeout:\n",
    "        elapsed = int(time.time() - start_time)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Check for remaining pods\n",
    "        result = run_kubectl([\n",
    "            \"get\", \"pods\",\n",
    "            \"-n\", NAMESPACE,\n",
    "            \"-l\", f\"ray.io/cluster={CLUSTER_NAME}\",\n",
    "            \"--no-headers\"\n",
    "        ], check=False)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        if result.returncode == 0:\n",
    "            lines = result.stdout.strip().split('\\n')\n",
    "            remaining = len([l for l in lines if l.strip()])\n",
    "            \n",
    "            if remaining == 0:\n",
    "                print(f\"✓ All pods terminated (took {elapsed}s)\\n\")\n",
    "                break\n",
    "            \n",
    "            print(f\"\\r[{elapsed:3d}s] Pods remaining: {remaining}\", end=\"\", flush=True)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        time.sleep(2)\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print(f\"\\n⚠ Some pods still terminating after {timeout}s\\n\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Final status\n",
    "    print(\"=\" * 80)\n",
    "    print(\"FINAL STATUS\")\n",
    "    print(\"=\" * 80)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Check RayCluster\n",
    "    result = run_kubectl([\n",
    "        \"get\", \"raycluster\", CLUSTER_NAME,\n",
    "        \"-n\", NAMESPACE\n",
    "    ], check=False)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    if result.returncode != 0 and \"NotFound\" in result.stderr:\n",
    "        print(\"\\n✓ RayCluster resource removed\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print(\"\\n⚠ RayCluster resource still exists\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Check pods\n",
    "    result = run_kubectl([\n",
    "        \"get\", \"pods\",\n",
    "        \"-n\", NAMESPACE,\n",
    "        \"-l\", f\"ray.io/cluster={CLUSTER_NAME}\",\n",
    "        \"--no-headers\"\n",
    "    ], check=False)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    if result.returncode == 0:\n",
    "        lines = [l for l in result.stdout.strip().split('\\n') if l.strip()]\n",
    "        if not lines:\n",
    "            print(\"✓ All pods cleaned up\")\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            print(f\"⚠ {len(lines)} pods still exist\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 80)\n",
    "\n",
    "verify_cleanup()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Test Complete! ✅\n",
    "\n",
    "If you saw:\n",
    "- ✓ RayCluster created\n",
    "- ✓ Cluster ready\n",
    "- ✓ Dashboard URL displayed\n",
    "- ✓ Cluster deleted\n",
    "- ✓ Cleanup verified\n",
    "\n",
    "Then **KubeRay with OpenShift AI configuration is working!**\n",
    "\n",
    "### What We Tested\n",
    "\n",
    "✅ RayCluster with CodeFlare-compatible configuration  \n",
    "✅ Correct Ray image (`quay.io/project-codeflare/ray:latest-py39-cu118`)  \n",
    "✅ Ray version 2.54.1  \n",
    "✅ ODH trusted CA certificate handling  \n",
    "✅ Proper lifecycle hooks  \n",
    "✅ Dashboard URL retrieval  \n",
    "✅ Clean cluster deletion  \n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Configuration Elements\n",
    "\n",
    "This configuration includes OpenShift AI / ODH best practices:\n",
    "- **CodeFlare Ray image**: Production-ready with proper dependencies\n",
    "- **Certificate trust**: ODH CA bundle mounts for secure networking\n",
